r\nI changed the URL to `https://curl.se/dev/` and added a `c.setopt(c.VERBOSE,1)`.\r\nThe output from `example/basicfirst.py`:\r\n```\r\nTesting PycURL/7.43.0.6 libcurl/7.75.0-DEV OpenSSL/3.0.0 (Schannel) (rustls) zlib/1.2.11 brotli/1.0.0 \r\nzstd/1.4.4 c-ares/1.17.0 WinIDN libssh2/1.9.0_DEV nghttp2/1.39.0 librtmp/2.3 Hyper/0.13.8\r\n....\r\n*  SSL certificate verify ok.\r\n* Time for the Hyper dance\r\n> GET /dev/ HTTP/2\r\n> Host: curl.se\r\n> User-Agent: PycURL/7.43.0.6 libcurl/7.75.0-DEV OpenSSL/3.0.0 (Schannel) (rustls) zlib/1.2.11 brotli/1.0.0  zstd/1.4.4 c-ares/1.17.0 WinIDN libssh2/1.9.0_DEV nghttp2/1.39.0 librtmp/2.3 Hyper/0.13.8\r\n> Accept: */*\r\n>\r\n< HTTP/2 200 OK\r\n* Closing connection 0\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"F:\\MingW32\\src\\inet\\curl\\pycurl\\examples\\basicfirst.py\", line 34, in <module>\r\n    c.perform()\r\npycurl.error: (23, '')\r\n```\r\n(`23 = CURLE_WRITE_ERROR`).\r\n\r\nBuilding libcurl without `-DUSE_HYPER` there is no issue with `https://curl.se/dev/`. So I'm not sure who's fault this is. \r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pycurl/pycurl/issues/666/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pycurl/pycurl/issues/666/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":4161619972,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDQxNjE2MTk5NzI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/curl/curl/issues/events/4161619972","actor":{"login":"bagder","id":177011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzAxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder","html_url":"https://github.com/bagder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bagder/gists{/gist_id}"